1035
01:09:15.877 --> 01:09:17.437
Hey, Bert. Sorry, Bert.

1036
01:09:17.517 --> 01:09:18.537
How you doing?

1037
01:09:29.937 --> 01:09:31.517
Don't worry about me.

1038
01:09:32.057 --> 01:09:33.157
Come on.

1039
01:09:33.617 --> 01:09:37.617
You wait outside and check them
and count them as we throw them out.

1040
01:09:43.037 --> 01:09:44.277
Don't count.

1041
01:09:56.477 --> 01:09:58.017
It's getting late.

1042
01:10:01.437 --> 01:10:04.137
Oh, honey, I was so afraid you'd get hurt.

1043
01:10:09.697 --> 01:10:13.057
And I'm not going to
see my darling anymore.

1044
01:10:13.637 --> 01:10:17.937
I'm sitting by the river
and I'm weeping all the day.

1045
01:10:20.217 --> 01:10:23.297
I love the old Kentucky show.

1046
01:10:23.957 --> 01:10:25.237
Oh, it's wonderful.

1047
01:10:25.317 --> 01:10:27.317
We got money and whiskey
and lovely ladies.

1048
01:10:27.397 --> 01:10:28.677
Just had a beautiful fight.

1049
01:10:28.757 --> 01:10:31.177
I tell you, we really ought to
be thankful for our blessings.

1050
01:10:31.257 --> 01:10:33.537
Ah, you've been reading that Bible again.

1051
01:10:33.617 --> 01:10:35.957
That's something I never thought I'd see.

1052
01:10:36.037 --> 01:10:38.137
What? A Bible with your name on it.

1053
01:10:38.217 --> 01:10:41.217
Now, where would you get a Bible?

1054
01:10:47.797 --> 01:10:48.817
Quartz!

1055
01:10:53.217 --> 01:10:55.477
Oh, Randy, stop him.

1056
01:10:55.677 --> 01:10:57.017
With what?

1057
01:10:57.237 --> 01:10:59.884
Where's he going? Has
he forgotten something?

1058
01:11:00.157 --> 01:11:01.317
No.

1059
01:11:09.917 --> 01:11:11.037
Penny!

1060
01:11:11.117 --> 01:11:13.677
What is wrong with the of late?

1061
01:11:13.777 --> 01:11:15.957
Tablecloths don't belong in there.

1062
01:11:16.857 --> 01:11:18.357
I'm sorry.

1063
01:11:31.397 --> 01:11:34.977
Oh, my God.

1064
01:11:58.217 --> 01:11:59.217
Quirk!

1065
01:11:59.737 --> 01:12:01.737
Unsaddle my horse, will you, kid?

1066
01:12:01.837 --> 01:12:02.837
Sure.

1067
01:12:03.597 --> 01:12:04.957
Want to board her for a while?

1068
01:12:05.037 --> 01:12:06.737
Of course. You're always welcome.

1069
01:12:06.817 --> 01:12:07.817
Quirk!

1070
01:12:08.377 --> 01:12:09.377
Hello!

1071
01:12:09.557 --> 01:12:11.777
Well, I haven't had a
decent meal since I left you.

1072
01:12:11.857 --> 01:12:12.697
Chocolate?

1073
01:12:12.777 --> 01:12:15.437
Not very good. The flour, you know.

1074
01:12:15.517 --> 01:12:17.997
Well, I'll just stick around
until you get one right.

1075
01:12:18.077 --> 01:12:20.837
I'll feed the chicken. So early, Penny?

1076
01:12:20.917 --> 01:12:21.917
Yes.

1077
01:12:22.117 --> 01:12:23.417
Help me, Court.

1078
01:12:30.357 --> 01:12:33.257
Does it take two to feed
a few chickens, Mother?

1079
01:12:34.137 --> 01:12:36.857
At times, Thomas, at times.

1080
01:12:37.197 --> 01:12:38.197
Remember?

1081
01:12:45.937 --> 01:12:47.637
You came back?

1082
01:12:48.557 --> 01:12:49.637
Yes.

1083
01:12:52.137 --> 01:12:53.137
Why?

1084
01:12:54.597 --> 01:12:56.437
I don't know exactly.

1085
01:12:56.937 --> 01:12:59.217
Why did you go away
without saying anything?

1086
01:12:59.297 --> 01:13:01.317
I don't know that exactly either.

1087
01:13:01.817 --> 01:13:04.417
I think it was because I frightened you.

1088
01:13:04.537 --> 01:13:08.596
I know that sounds strange that I
should frighten you, but I mean it.

1089
01:13:09.197 --> 01:13:14.137
You were frightened because I was stupid,
and you thought that living with me would

1090
01:13:14.217 --> 01:13:16.617
be tiresome and dull after a while.

1091
01:13:17.497 --> 01:13:22.357
Tiresome and dull because all I knew,
Ray, since a baby here on the farm was our

1092
01:13:22.437 --> 01:13:28.257
belief that people love, marry,
and stay together forever after that.

1093
01:13:28.917 --> 01:13:33.417
I'm not such a fool not to know that
outside and worldly places people love it.

1094
01:13:33.497 --> 01:13:37.137
It doesn't have to follow that they
marry and stay together forever.

1095
01:13:37.217 --> 01:13:39.357
I know that sometimes they separate.

1096
01:13:39.437 --> 01:13:40.497
Are you ever going to run, Donna?

1097
01:13:40.577 --> 01:13:44.337
Let me talk. No, Court, that's what you
were afraid of, that I tied myself around

1098
01:13:44.417 --> 01:13:45.417
your neck,

1099
01:13:46.117 --> 01:13:47.377
be rid of me.

1100
01:13:47.517 --> 01:13:50.877
And I made up my mind if you
came back, I'd tell you this,

1101
01:13:50.957 --> 01:13:53.486
that whenever you want,
course, you can be.

1102
01:13:53.777 --> 01:13:55.957
If I go away, you go with me.

1103
01:13:56.197 --> 01:13:58.457
If I go away, they go with me.

1104
01:14:13.177 --> 01:14:15.457
I used to be an engine fighter.

1105
01:14:16.797 --> 01:14:19.757
Just can't help walking up soft on people.

1106
01:14:20.857 --> 01:14:22.197
Morning, Missy.

1107
01:14:22.877 --> 01:14:26.457
This young man been doing any
traveling since I was here last?

1108
01:14:26.537 --> 01:14:30.037
I lost a big herd a few days ago.

1109
01:14:31.437 --> 01:14:33.917
Why, Missy, cat got your tongue?

1110
01:14:33.997 --> 01:14:36.857
Why ask her? You know I've been traveling.

1111
01:14:36.977 --> 01:14:39.117
You look in the carral to
see how my horse shaped up.

1112
01:14:39.197 --> 01:14:40.477
I did just that.

1113
01:14:40.557 --> 01:14:42.937
And he sure covered a lot of country.

1114
01:14:43.037 --> 01:14:44.997
He's a right weary animal.

1115
01:14:46.357 --> 01:14:49.897
I just wanted to see would
the young lady lie for you?

1116
01:14:53.657 --> 01:14:55.377
I was going to.

1117
01:14:55.717 --> 01:14:57.617
You've been over Castle Verdeway?

1118
01:14:57.697 --> 01:15:00.873
I've been to Rimrock, and
I got witnesses to prove it.

1119
01:15:01.037 --> 01:15:02.137
Witnesses?

1120
01:15:02.217 --> 01:15:03.677
For instance?

1121
01:15:03.797 --> 01:15:05.277
Randy McCall.

1122
01:15:06.077 --> 01:15:07.717
Christine Taylor.

1123
01:15:08.117 --> 01:15:10.217
That's what I call witnesses.

1124
01:15:11.177 --> 01:15:12.617
Who else?

1125
01:15:12.997 --> 01:15:14.937
Lala Neal, I suppose.

1126
01:15:15.237 --> 01:15:18.017
She'd make a good alibi witness for you.

1127
01:15:18.337 --> 01:15:21.317
Randy, Christine, and Lala.

1128
01:15:21.937 --> 01:15:23.917
There's three to draw, too.

1129
01:15:25.077 --> 01:15:27.437
So Lala saw you there too, huh?

1130
01:15:28.357 --> 01:15:29.357
Yes.

1131
01:15:34.997 --> 01:15:36.837
Come here, junkhead.

1132
01:15:37.077 --> 01:15:39.297
You dollar and a half brush jumper.

1133
01:15:39.557 --> 01:15:40.557
Hmm.

1134
01:15:45.857 --> 01:15:48.437
Well, there's a mystic in, Quirt.

1135
01:15:49.297 --> 01:15:50.977
But I'm patient.

1136
01:15:51.357 --> 01:15:54.217
That's what hangs all
you fellas in the end.

1137
01:15:54.797 --> 01:15:56.297
I'm patient.

1138
01:16:05.997 --> 01:16:07.117
Lyla.

1139
01:16:09.777 --> 01:16:12.637
You talked about her
when you were delirious.

1140
01:16:56.697 --> 01:16:58.197
Oh, no.

1141
01:17:48.617 --> 01:17:52.017
I wish my hair were...

1142
01:17:53.137 --> 01:17:55.997
Hers was like corn silk, you say.

1143
01:18:22.177 --> 01:18:24.657
There's a sight I never thought I'd see.

1144
01:18:24.877 --> 01:18:27.057
Quirt Evans behind the plow.

1145
01:18:28.317 --> 01:18:30.277
Pony walks as soft as you do.

1146
01:18:30.357 --> 01:18:31.717
I taught him.

1147
01:18:32.557 --> 01:18:34.857
Oh, I figured you'd have hurt him.

1148
01:18:35.697 --> 01:18:37.817
Except you were thinking too hard.

1149
01:18:39.017 --> 01:18:42.657
Haven't you got some real
important business to attend to?

1150
01:18:43.037 --> 01:18:45.017
Someplace else? Sure.

1151
01:18:45.177 --> 01:18:48.236
But I always like to keep
track of your whereabouts.

1152
01:18:57.237 --> 01:18:58.757
You know, Quirt,

1153
01:18:59.497 --> 01:19:02.897
I always figured on using
a new rope and hanging you.

1154
01:19:03.877 --> 01:19:06.677
Because I kind of respected you.

1155
01:19:07.297 --> 01:19:09.617
You never took the best of things.

1156
01:19:10.097 --> 01:19:12.897
And all your men went down looking at you.

1157
01:19:12.977 --> 01:19:14.857
Don't mind your own business.

1158
01:19:15.237 --> 01:19:16.857
I usually do.

1159
01:19:17.777 --> 01:19:22.397
It's a shame things don't always
turn out the way they should.

1160
01:19:24.117 --> 01:19:28.517
Now that little gal should
marry some young fella

1161
01:19:29.017 --> 01:19:31.637
who know what to do with that plow.

1162
01:19:31.897 --> 01:19:35.197
Why don't you kick up
that horse and move on?

1163
01:19:35.437 --> 01:19:38.217
Some young fella would
raise a lot of grain.

1164
01:19:40.397 --> 01:19:42.097
Cows, sheep,

1165
01:19:42.457 --> 01:19:43.837
and kids.

1166
01:19:45.077 --> 01:19:46.977
the kind of a fella that

1167
01:19:47.497 --> 01:19:49.877
she'd always know where he was.

1168
01:19:50.317 --> 01:19:52.497
Do I have to run you off?

1169
01:19:52.657 --> 01:19:54.377
Well, now I'll tell you.

1170
01:19:55.097 --> 01:19:59.557
I never have been run off no
place yet where I aim to stay.

1171
01:20:00.657 --> 01:20:03.257
But it just so happens I gotta be gone.

1172
01:20:09.077 --> 01:20:10.377
No, Quirt.

1173
01:20:11.397 --> 01:20:13.897
You don't raid a new rope with me.

1174
01:20:35.257 --> 01:20:36.877
Look, uh...

1175
01:20:38.797 --> 01:20:42.237
There's a lot of fouperawe and
nonsense have to go with it.

1176
01:20:42.317 --> 01:20:46.417
I'm not going to stand for a lot of
dressing up and a batch of jabbering people

1177
01:20:46.497 --> 01:20:49.262
looking at me just because
I'm getting married.

1178
01:20:50.417 --> 01:20:51.417
Cory,

1179
01:20:52.317 --> 01:20:53.877
come along with me.

1180
01:20:54.177 --> 01:20:55.657
Well, yes or no?

1181
01:20:55.777 --> 01:20:57.057
Come along.

1182
01:20:59.397 --> 01:21:00.837
Picking blackberries?

1183
01:21:00.917 --> 01:21:01.917
Mm-hmm.

1184
01:21:02.797 --> 01:21:03.877
All right.

1185
01:21:39.957 --> 01:21:41.517
Never did like blackberries.

1186
01:21:41.597 --> 01:21:43.037
Now I know I was right.

1187
01:21:44.637 --> 01:21:46.457
Too much work connected with it.

1188
01:21:46.537 --> 01:21:48.277
I'll get some more for her.

1189
01:22:07.897 --> 01:22:09.517
Look out, there's a wasp on that petunia.

1190
01:22:09.597 --> 01:22:10.857
Don't kill him.

1191
01:22:11.337 --> 01:22:16.097
Well, it's all right for you to trust
wasps and people, but he might have known I

1192
01:22:16.177 --> 01:22:18.942
don't trust him and
decided to take first bite.

1193
01:22:19.197 --> 01:22:22.432
And incidentally, that's not
a petunia, that's a daisy.

1194
01:22:22.617 --> 01:22:24.137
That's a petunia.

1195
01:22:24.457 --> 01:22:26.697
Petunia, daisy, daisy, petunia.

1196
01:22:27.857 --> 01:22:29.117
Court Evans.

1197
01:22:30.137 --> 01:22:31.237
Oh, nothing.

1198
01:22:31.317 --> 01:22:33.457
I just like the sound of it.

1199
01:22:33.697 --> 01:22:34.697
Court.

1200
01:22:34.857 --> 01:22:37.177
Where'd they ever get such an odd name?

1201
01:22:37.697 --> 01:22:40.168
A fellow who half raised me gave it to me.

1202
01:22:40.477 --> 01:22:43.557
He found me somewhere
along the big cattle trail.

1203
01:22:44.037 --> 01:22:47.637
Folks had been bushwhacked
by Indians, I guess.

1204
01:22:47.997 --> 01:22:50.697
He was a big fellow, cattleman.

1205
01:22:51.057 --> 01:22:53.637
Swung a wide loop in his
younger days, I think.

1206
01:22:53.717 --> 01:22:54.837
Wide loop?

1207
01:22:54.977 --> 01:22:58.330
Well, wasn't too careful whose
calf he threw his rope at.

1208
01:22:59.137 --> 01:23:02.037
Most of the old cattlemen were like that.

1209
01:23:02.477 --> 01:23:03.997
He raised me.

1210
01:23:04.137 --> 01:23:05.757
He was quite a guy.

1211
01:23:05.877 --> 01:23:07.697
His name was Walt Ennis.

1212
01:23:08.597 --> 01:23:12.277
He was downed in a gambling place.

1213
01:23:12.937 --> 01:23:15.697
The fellow grabbed his
gun arm just as he drew.

1214
01:23:15.777 --> 01:23:17.037
It was murder.

1215
01:23:18.457 --> 01:23:19.877
Stop it.

1216
01:23:20.797 --> 01:23:22.137
Then what?

1217
01:23:22.477 --> 01:23:25.717
Well, I just bounced
around from place to place.

1218
01:23:26.617 --> 01:23:27.957
Court Ennis.

1219
01:23:58.517 --> 01:24:00.517
I don't see any gun. I know him.

1220
01:24:00.597 --> 01:24:02.037
He's got a gun all right.

1221
01:24:02.117 --> 01:24:03.437
I know him.

1222
01:24:06.257 --> 01:24:07.637
Yeah!

1223
01:24:45.317 --> 01:24:48.617
Oh, yeah.

1224
01:26:19.197 --> 01:26:22.497
Thank you.

1225
01:26:58.617 --> 01:27:00.457
Well, what are we waiting for?

1226
01:27:01.337 --> 01:27:02.697
Nothing, I guess.

1227
01:27:03.237 --> 01:27:04.777
Let's find a saloon.

1228
01:27:09.697 --> 01:27:12.517
You don't have to be
worried about Penny, Mother.

1229
01:27:12.597 --> 01:27:15.977
Oh, I can't help
worrying about it, Johnny.

1230
01:27:17.537 --> 01:27:20.517
Get that doctor and burn
up the road both ways.

1231
01:28:07.497 --> 01:28:08.797
Drink.

1232
01:28:11.717 --> 01:28:13.457
It's amazing.

1233
01:28:14.217 --> 01:28:17.797
The varied uses to which men put alcohol.

1234
01:28:18.217 --> 01:28:22.657
To each different individual,
it's either a stimulant, a depressant,

1235
01:28:22.737 --> 01:28:24.297
or an anodyne.

1236
01:28:24.377 --> 01:28:27.057
Just now I'm using it as an anodyne.

1237
01:28:27.917 --> 01:28:29.637
Get to the point.

1238
01:28:31.317 --> 01:28:37.077
The practice of medicine is one of the
most infuriating professions known to man.

1239
01:28:38.137 --> 01:28:42.937
It takes 30 years of experience to
teach you that in the final analysis,

1240
01:28:43.017 --> 01:28:46.357
there's nothing to do but stand and watch.

1241
01:28:51.357 --> 01:28:56.177
If she has a lucid moment,
you'd better speak to her.

1242
01:29:09.297 --> 01:29:11.997
I'm not trying to argue
you out of anything,

1243
01:29:12.517 --> 01:29:14.752
but maybe you ought to stop and think.

1244
01:29:19.357 --> 01:29:21.257
She wouldn't like this, Quirt.

1245
01:29:22.077 --> 01:29:25.697
I'm not arguing for or
against her point of view.

1246
01:29:25.777 --> 01:29:29.997
But I know that to her, the world's worst
tragedy would be that you should kill a

1247
01:29:30.077 --> 01:29:30.797
man.

1248
01:29:30.877 --> 01:29:34.877
Of course, you could argue logically that
she wouldn't know whether you'd killed him

1249
01:29:34.957 --> 01:29:35.957
or not.

1250
01:29:36.257 --> 01:29:37.937
I think she'd know.

1251
01:29:38.697 --> 01:29:41.797
Any discussion has to have
at least two participants.

1252
01:29:41.877 --> 01:29:45.057
Of course, if you
refuse to answer me, I...

1253
01:29:46.217 --> 01:29:47.217
Quirt!

1254
01:29:51.617 --> 01:29:57.057
If I felt cynical, this would be a good
opportunity to observe that we're about to

1255
01:29:57.137 --> 01:30:01.117
see a perfect example of
an eye for an eye, etc.

1256
01:30:02.477 --> 01:30:05.517
Unfortunately, I can't
quote chapter and verse.

1257
01:30:05.897 --> 01:30:08.457
And I'm too tired to be cynical.

1258
01:30:16.977 --> 01:30:17.817
Father!

1259
01:30:17.897 --> 01:30:19.597
Father! Come upstairs!

1260
01:30:21.737 --> 01:30:23.017
But they are very ill.

1261
01:30:23.097 --> 01:30:24.677
They must not be moving about.

1262
01:30:24.757 --> 01:30:25.717
Mother, I've got to go to him.

1263
01:30:25.797 --> 01:30:27.217
They must get back into bed.

1264
01:30:27.297 --> 01:30:28.637
But he needs me.

1265
01:30:28.717 --> 01:30:31.017
This is insanity. I told
you to keep her in bed.

1266
01:30:31.097 --> 01:30:32.477
You want to commit suicide?

1267
01:30:32.557 --> 01:30:35.263
You don't stay under
those covers, young lady.

1268
01:30:39.577 --> 01:30:41.097
There's no fever.

1269
01:30:41.337 --> 01:30:43.357
Well, they must do what the doctor says.

1270
01:30:43.437 --> 01:30:44.537
Mother, please.

1271
01:30:44.617 --> 01:30:46.357
I can't understand it.

1272
01:30:47.517 --> 01:30:49.717
I can't understand it at all.

1273
01:30:49.797 --> 01:30:52.697
There must be some logical
scientific explanation.

1274
01:30:52.777 --> 01:30:55.777
I'm too old to start
believing in miracles.

1275
01:30:55.917 --> 01:30:57.357
Wrap her in blankets.

1276
01:31:20.057 --> 01:31:22.477
The other two haven't had me covered.

1277
01:31:22.997 --> 01:31:26.477
I never let that Hondo
Jeffries pistol whip me.

1278
01:31:26.917 --> 01:31:29.497
Wait till Kurt Evans hears about this.

1279
01:31:30.317 --> 01:31:33.737
He and me will take the starch
out of the whole caboodle of it.

1280
01:31:33.817 --> 01:31:35.397
Why, Kurt and me once...

1281
01:31:35.477 --> 01:31:40.697
Well, it wasn't Dodge City several years
back, when the Erks and Clintons were

1282
01:31:40.777 --> 01:31:44.117
gunning it. Well, me and Quirt...

1283
01:31:47.537 --> 01:31:48.817
Come here.

1284
01:31:49.197 --> 01:31:50.817
Yes, Mr. Evans.

1285
01:32:01.497 --> 01:32:02.977
Olorado, Stevens.

1286
01:32:03.217 --> 01:32:04.457
He's in the Eagle.

1287
01:32:04.537 --> 01:32:07.017
And that pistol-ripping Hondo's with him.

1288
01:32:10.217 --> 01:32:11.817
Take him a message.

1289
01:32:16.057 --> 01:32:17.057
Hey.

1290
01:32:17.437 --> 01:32:19.077
Buy the boys a drink.

1291
01:32:19.377 --> 01:32:20.377
Celebrating?

1292
01:32:20.957 --> 01:32:21.957
Sure.

1293
01:32:22.037 --> 01:32:23.237
Why not?

1294
01:32:23.697 --> 01:32:26.237
Don't you ever get excited when
you make a big win like this?

1295
01:32:26.317 --> 01:32:29.729
Why get excited? Sometimes
you win and sometimes you lose.

1296
01:32:30.317 --> 01:32:32.397
Don't get excited, gentlemen.

1297
01:32:42.497 --> 01:32:44.477
I ain't looking for trouble.

1298
01:32:45.117 --> 01:32:47.157
I'm just a carry on a message.

1299
01:32:47.237 --> 01:32:47.817
Yeah?

1300
01:32:47.897 --> 01:32:49.197
What is it?

1301
01:32:49.317 --> 01:32:51.317
He said to come out in the street.

1302
01:32:51.417 --> 01:32:53.057
He's waiting for you.

1303
01:32:53.137 --> 01:32:54.217
Who says?

1304
01:32:55.057 --> 01:32:56.237
Kurt Evans.

1305
01:33:03.317 --> 01:33:04.737
What is this, a joke?

1306
01:33:05.097 --> 01:33:07.177
Quirt Evans is...

1307
01:33:07.297 --> 01:33:10.650
Take a look out in the street
to see if it really is him.

1308
01:33:14.337 --> 01:33:16.219
Jack, take a look in the street.

1309
01:33:33.597 --> 01:33:37.857
There's a tall hombre in a black
hat standing at the blacksmith shop.

1310
01:33:43.197 --> 01:33:44.817
Mind if I use the back door, Pete?

1311
01:33:44.897 --> 01:33:46.017
So long, Pete.

1312
01:34:04.817 --> 01:34:07.417
Well, this cat's got nine lives.

1313
01:34:09.897 --> 01:34:11.817
Maybe old Quirt's part cat.

1314
01:34:11.977 --> 01:34:15.859
He also said he was curious to
know how much whiskey it would take

1315
01:34:16.237 --> 01:34:18.237
to build up your nerve to come out.

1316
01:34:18.317 --> 01:34:19.757
You fixing to get your ears pinned back?

1317
01:34:19.837 --> 01:34:22.137
There's a better pair of ears out in the
street if you want to pin somebody's ears

1318
01:34:22.217 --> 01:34:23.217
back.

1319
01:34:23.617 --> 01:34:25.137
Here, you drink this.

1320
01:34:26.517 --> 01:34:27.517
Sure.

1321
01:34:28.097 --> 01:34:30.037
I don't have to stand near you.

1322
01:34:30.237 --> 01:34:31.237
Come on.

1323
01:34:32.497 --> 01:34:33.917
sharpshooting marshals around town.

1324
01:34:33.997 --> 01:34:36.585
Oh, I saw him right
out of town an hour ago.

1325
01:34:38.317 --> 01:34:39.437
That's good.

1326
01:34:39.517 --> 01:34:42.137
Wouldn't want him around
here to spoil our play.

1327
01:34:42.217 --> 01:34:42.757
Yeah.

1328
01:34:42.837 --> 01:34:45.537
I bet that's just exactly
how you meant that.

1329
01:35:16.977 --> 01:35:20.597
Oh, my God.

1330
01:36:15.197 --> 01:36:17.097
Where?

1331
01:37:14.617 --> 01:37:16.937
Quirt, step away from those women.

1332
01:37:23.977 --> 01:37:26.057
Why don't you turn around, Quirt?

1333
01:37:51.657 --> 01:37:53.917
Nothing ever works out right.

1334
01:38:00.897 --> 01:38:03.217
I had them dead to rights.

1335
01:38:03.537 --> 01:38:05.577
They got the Baker stage.

1336
01:38:05.977 --> 01:38:08.497
So I figured I'd watch the ruckus.

1337
01:38:08.817 --> 01:38:10.497
You down them.

1338
01:38:10.937 --> 01:38:12.777
And I'd hang you.

1339
01:38:13.197 --> 01:38:19.597
Sort of killing three hawks
with one stone, so to speak.

1340
01:38:20.917 --> 01:38:23.997
And nothing, nothing ever works out right.

1341
01:38:26.077 --> 01:38:30.157
Not to Mr. Pinport, but I'm patient.

1342
01:38:30.817 --> 01:38:33.457
It's only a matter of time and I hang you.

1343
01:38:34.357 --> 01:38:35.837
Not me, mister.

1344
01:38:36.657 --> 01:38:38.737
From now on, I'm a farmer.

1345
01:38:54.877 --> 01:38:56.217
That quirk.

1346
01:39:02.057 --> 01:39:03.737
Say, quirk might need that.

1347
01:39:03.817 --> 01:39:04.817
No.

1348
01:39:05.257 --> 01:39:08.017
Only a man who carries
a gun ever needs one.

1349
01:39:08.277 --> 01:39:10.042
What are you gonna do with it?

1350
01:39:10.657 --> 01:39:12.657
Hang it on the wall in Morpheus.

1351
01:39:13.057 --> 01:39:14.617
With a new rope.

